-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- 0040 — EVERY WATER ANSWERS ITS SEA
--        A sea-membership raster on the same 0.25° grid as the water itself: every navigable
--        cell carries the ordinal of the sea it is in, so a fleet at ANY water point still has
--        a region — the thing piracy, hazards and the by-sea NPC design (OWNER_REQUESTS row 43)
--        are keyed on, and the thing free sailing would otherwise silently switch off.
--        GENERATED by scripts/build-sea-raster.mjs — do not hand-edit; edit the data or the
--        generator and run it again. Boundaries are Natural Earth ne_10m_geography_marine_polys
--        (public domain, same source family as the coastline), NOT the hand-placed label
--        centroids of data/seas.json, which its own note marks unsurveyed. Water bearing an NE
--        name we do not model joins the nearest named sea BY WATER (BFS through water cells),
--        so nothing leaks across land. §7B decisions are in the generator header.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
--
-- THE NUMBERS, from this generation: 647913 water cells; 647226 carry a sea;
-- 687 do not — 628 cells near (41.8, 50.7); 28 cells near (48.9, -123.6); 8 cells near (66.1, -162.8); 8 cells near (9.7, -71.6); 4 cells near (-53.1, -70.6); 3 cells near (-53.9, -71.4) — 13 landlocked pool(s) no sea route reaches (the largest is the Caspian).
-- Ports checked against their cell: 238 in the data, 228 in the chain at
-- this position (10 island ports in data/ports.json await their own seeding slice);
-- disagreements with the declared sea among the chain's ports: 17
-- (each one asserted below BY NAME — a silent drift of this list is a red apply).
--
-- Depends on: 0002 (public.seas, public.ports), 0003 (the seed), 0036 (SEA_PLACE rows).

-- ── 1. the seas learn their ordinal, their danger tier and their character ────────────────────
-- raster_ordinal: the byte value of this sea in public.sea_cells. 1-based position in
-- data/seas.json array order, which is append-only (the seas.json note says so).
-- danger_level: the authored WHERE-keyed threat tier (1 home waters … 5 deadly) the owner
-- specified for NPC encounters — "different npcs in different areas of the sea - different
-- levels". READ BY NO RULE TODAY (2026-08-24): named readers are the NPC/encounter system
-- (OWNER_REQUESTS row 43) and any level-gated hazard content. Stated plainly, the takes_effect
-- discipline of 0015/0016: an authored field nothing reads yet is marked, never implied live.
-- note: the sea's character in plain words — a NAME, not a sentence (UI_DIRECTION). Same
-- posture: no rule reads it yet; the map label / compendium is its named reader.
alter table public.seas
  add column raster_ordinal smallint,
  add column danger_level   int,
  add column note           text;

